<P class=3D"version">                &nbsp;|&nbsp;                       =
         =20
   Version: Simply Fortran 1.44                             =
</P></HEADER>
<P class=3D"sectionHeading">Pros</P>
<P class=3D"sectionText">Uses gfortran with mingw, so anything you do in =
fortran=20
using Linux, osx, or Cygwin should work.  It's nice to have a simple to =
use IDE=20
that automatically compiles all the necessary modules and objects.  This =
is by=20
far the best and simplest to use fortran IDE I have found for windows.  =
If you=20
are designing HPC software on a windows machine this is a good place to=20
start.</P>
<P class=3D"sectionHeading">Cons</P>
<P class=3D"sectionText">I can't find much, but I have only been using =
the program=20
for about a day so far.  I'll add an update if I find anything worth=20
mentioning.</P>
