<P class=3D"title">"Great for Fortran 90/95 users"</P>
<P class=3D"author">                                    June 13, 2012    =
         =20
                                      &nbsp;|&nbsp;                      =
       =20
                      By <A class=3D"noluke" =
href=3D"http://www.cnet.com/profiles/gat0gelat0/">=20
gat0gelat0</A>                             </P>
<P class=3D"review-author-mobile">                                    =
2012-06-13=20
00:10:15                                                    =
&nbsp;|&nbsp;       =20
                                            By gat0gelat0                =
       =20
     </P>
<P class=3D"version">                &nbsp;|&nbsp;                       =
         =20
   Version: Simply Fortran 1.30                             =
</P></HEADER>
<P class=3D"sectionHeading">Pros</P>
<P class=3D"sectionText">Very easy to use. The 'Project' feature is cool =
- keeps=20
all files relevant to a project in one place and make them available for =
view=20
and edit. The editor is user friendly - color codes for different =
statement=20
types makes it easy to write code. Code, binary data files etc. are also =

portable, as long as the system is of the same type (e.g. 64 bit).</P>
<P class=3D"sectionHeading">Cons</P>
<P class=3D"sectionText">Sometimes the compiler gives error warnings =
where there=20
shouldn't be any (e.g. 'possible conversion of real*8 to real*4, when =
double=20
precision has been declared - it'll let you compile and run anyway and =
it will=20
run fine if the code is really ok). Also wish the Gnuplot graphing tools =
were=20
integrated into this package. I generate data files using SF, which I =
then plot=20
using Gnuplot, separately. Wish there was an integrated Gnuplot menu =
within the=20
same interface especially since I write and maintain a Gnuplot script =
file as=20
part of a Project; now if only I could click on the script and Gnuplot =
would=20
automatically open up and plot it. :)</P>
<P class=3D"sectionHeading">Summary</P>
<P class=3D"sectionText">Very worth it.</P>
